{"id":"0db76c21ee915f76","group":"62","path":"62/62-lem-ATR-uniqueness.md","title":"Uniqueness of Arithmetical Recursion Hierarchies","display":"lem-ATR-uniqueness — Uniqueness of Arithmetical Recursion Hierarchies","type":"lemma","metadata":{"type":"lemma","book":"Subsystems of Second Order Arithmetic (Simpson)","book_abbrev":"62","label":"62-lem-ATR-uniqueness","aliases":["62-lem-ATR-uniqueness"],"display":"lem-ATR-uniqueness — Uniqueness of Arithmetical Recursion Hierarchies","depends_on":["[[62-df-ACA0]]","[[62-df-WellOrder]]","[[62-df-recursion-hierarchy]]","[[62-df-L2]]","[[62-df-derivability]]","[[62-thm-ACA0-transfinite-induction]]"],"source":"Simpson, 2nd edition (2009), Lemma V.2.3","source_pages":[174,175],"source_pdf_pages":[192,193]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"lemma"},{"key":"book","html":"Subsystems of Second Order Arithmetic (Simpson)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"62"},{"key":"label","html":"62-lem-ATR-uniqueness"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>62-lem-ATR-uniqueness</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"lem-ATR-uniqueness — Uniqueness of Arithmetical Recursion Hierarchies"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"35af454d9caa8c9d\" href=\"?note=35af454d9caa8c9d\" title=\"62-df-ACA0\">62-df-ACA0</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"649faa9c6d69237b\" href=\"?note=649faa9c6d69237b\" title=\"62-df-WellOrder\">62-df-WellOrder</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"0c50226ab37e9ce8\" href=\"?note=0c50226ab37e9ce8\" title=\"62-df-recursion-hierarchy\">62-df-recursion-hierarchy</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"4c6d2d9f1999915f\" href=\"?note=4c6d2d9f1999915f\" title=\"62-df-L2\">62-df-L2</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"98c3cbeb95500b53\" href=\"?note=98c3cbeb95500b53\" title=\"62-df-derivability\">62-df-derivability</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"9853288b97e63a4f\" href=\"?note=9853288b97e63a4f\" title=\"62-thm-ACA0-transfinite-induction\">62-thm-ACA0-transfinite-induction</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source","html":"Simpson, 2nd edition (2009), Lemma V.2.3"},{"key":"source_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>174</span><span>175</span></div>"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>192</span><span>193</span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p>理论和良序见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"35af454d9caa8c9d\" href=\"?note=35af454d9caa8c9d\" title=\"62-df-ACA0\">62-df-ACA0</a>、<a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-8\" data-note=\"649faa9c6d69237b\" href=\"?note=649faa9c6d69237b\" title=\"62-df-WellOrder\">62-df-WellOrder</a>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf H_\\theta\">\\(\\mathsf H_\\theta\\)</span> 及其新鲜变量条件见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-9\" data-note=\"0c50226ab37e9ce8\" href=\"?note=0c50226ab37e9ce8\" title=\"62-df-recursion-hierarchy\">62-df-recursion-hierarchy</a>；UC、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\vdash_{S_2}\">\\(\\vdash_{S_2}\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-10\" data-note=\"4c6d2d9f1999915f\" href=\"?note=4c6d2d9f1999915f\" title=\"62-df-L2\">62-df-L2</a>、<a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-11\" data-note=\"98c3cbeb95500b53\" href=\"?note=98c3cbeb95500b53\" title=\"62-df-derivability\">62-df-derivability</a>；归纳规则见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-12\" data-note=\"9853288b97e63a4f\" href=\"?note=9853288b97e63a4f\" title=\"62-thm-ACA0-transfinite-induction\">62-thm-ACA0-transfinite-induction</a>。θ 为所引用接口允许的算术公式。</p>\n<p>上游理论为 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ACA}_0\">\\(\\mathrm{ACA}_0\\)</span>，序谓词为 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{WO}(W,R)\">\\(\\mathrm{WO}(W,R)\\)</span>。</p>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"K\">\\(K\\)</span> 是不同于 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H,W,R,Z\">\\(H,W,R,Z\\)</span> 及 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\bar A\">\\(\\bar A\\)</span> 的集合变量，且 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"K\\notin\\mathrm{FV}_2(\\theta)\">\\(K\\notin\\mathrm{FV}_2(\\theta)\\)</span>；两次 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathsf H_\\theta\">\\(\\mathsf H_\\theta\\)</span> 调用使用同一个 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\theta\">\\(\\theta\\)</span> 和同一套数、集合参数。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{lem\\text{-}ATR\\text{-}uniqueness}\\vdash\\;\\mathrm{ACA}_0\\vdash_{S_2}\\operatorname{UC}\\bigl[(\\mathrm{WO}(W,R)\\land\\mathsf H_\\theta(W,R,H;\\bar u,\\bar A)\\land\\mathsf H_\\theta(W,R,K;\\bar u,\\bar A))\\to H=K\\bigr].\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{lem\\text{-}ATR\\text{-}uniqueness}\\vdash\\;\\mathrm{ACA}_0\\vdash_{S_2}\\operatorname{UC}\\bigl[(\\mathrm{WO}(W,R)\\land\\mathsf H_\\theta(W,R,H;\\bar u,\\bar A)\\land\\mathsf H_\\theta(W,R,K;\\bar u,\\bar A))\\to H=K\\bigr].\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>对阶段 a 作算术超限归纳：若所有严格前驱截面相同，则前驱汇总集相同；两边在同一参数下应用同一个 θ，故第 a 截面相同。载体外无元素，由外延性得 H=K。ACA₀ 证明“至多一个”，不证明每个层级都有结果；后者需要 ATR。</p>\n<p>来源：第二版（2009），Lemma V.2.3；纸面页 174, 175；PDF 页 192, 193。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"62-df-ACA0","status":"resolved","id":"35af454d9caa8c9d","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[62-df-ACA0]]","embed":false},{"target":"62-df-WellOrder","status":"resolved","id":"649faa9c6d69237b","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[62-df-WellOrder]]","embed":false},{"target":"62-df-recursion-hierarchy","status":"resolved","id":"0c50